&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education: Bachelor’s degree with a focus in Accounting, Finance, or a highly quantitative field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience: 3+ years of progressive accounting experience, ideally combining public accounting (Big 4/National) with a fast-growing technology, telecommunications, or CPaaS environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Accounting: Solid foundational knowledge of US GAAP, operational month-end close structures, and balance sheet reconciliations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data Mastery: Advanced Excel/Google Sheets capabilities. You must be comfortable manipulating massive, complex, and sometimes non-linear billing datasets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automation: Hands-on experience using AI and automation tools like Alteryx, UiPath, Gemini and NotebookLM – tell us what you’ve built!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mindset: Extreme ownership, structural organization, and a knack for solving ambiguous, messy operational data problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communication: Flawless written and verbal communication skills in English, with the ability to explain complex variance drivers to non-finance operational partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certified Public Accountant (CPA), Chartered Accountant, or local equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience handling carrier relations, telecom accounting, or high-volume usage-based vendor structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hand-on experience working within major enterprise systems (e.g., Oracle Fusion, NetSuite, Zuora, BlackLine).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leveraging analytical tools (SQL, Python, or advanced data visualization suites) to automate repetitive data reconciliations.&lt;/li&gt;
