&lt;p&gt;We use Artificial Intelligence (AI) to help make our hiring process efficient. That said, every hiring decision is made by real Twilions!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Also, while we are a remote-first company, you may be asked to report in person on an ad-hoc basis for team gatherings, functional off-sites or customer meetings.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;See yourself at Twilio&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join the team as Twilio’s next Senior Field Enablement Business Partner&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Twilio is seeking a Senior Field Enablement Partner to join our Global Go-To-Market (GTM) Enablement team. Reporting directly to the Senior Manager of GTM Specialist Enablement, you will act as a critical strategic partner to our Global Customer Services (GCS) organization as we transform our enablement model and scale the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you won&#39;t just deliver training—you’ll drive performance, productivity, and revenue effectiveness. You will design, localize, and roll out high-impact enablement strategies, programs, and tools that equip GCS to be successful. If you thrive in dynamic, fast-paced environments, love building from the ground up, and take pride in seeing the direct business impact of your work, this role is for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Act as a Strategic Consultant:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner directly with GCS leadership to analyze qualitative and quantitative performance data, identifying skill gaps and defining key competencies to deploy targeted enablement solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliver High-Impact Learning:&lt;/strong&gt; Facilitate interactive virtual instructor-led (vILT) and in-person enablement sessions tailored to specific field roles and audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Program Execution &amp;amp; Adoption: &lt;/strong&gt;Collaboratively plan, prioritize, and execute GCS enablement roadmaps while ensuring strong pre- and post-program evaluation metrics and long-term adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Co-Design Modern Curriculum:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with the Learning Experience Design (LXD) team to establish clear learning objectives grounded in adult learning theory and measurable business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optimize &amp;amp; Iterate Content:&lt;/strong&gt; Continually evaluate curriculum effectiveness, proposing data-backed updates, fresh content, and updates to internal knowledge bases and weekly enablement communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maintain Competitive Edge:&lt;/strong&gt; Stay ahead of industry trends, market shifts, and competitor products to ensure field teams are equipped to differentiate Twilio effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Twilio values diverse experiences from all kinds of industries, and we encourage everyone who meets the required qualifications to apply. If your career is just starting or hasn&#39;t followed a traditional path, don&#39;t let that stop you from considering Twilio. We are always looking for people who will bring something new to the table!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;*Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of total experience in services/sales enablement, services/sales operations, or direct professional services, with 3+ years in a strategic enablement or business partner role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven Track Record: Demonstrated success driving measurable performance impact and ROI through field enablement programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domain Expertise: Deep understanding of the B2B sales/services cycle within SaaS or complex enterprise tech environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modern Tech Stack Proficiency: Hands-on experience with enablement platforms (e.g., Highspot, Gong), Learning Management Systems (LMS), and CRMs (e.g., Salesforce).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Instructional Grounding: Strong understanding of adult learning theory and practical application of frameworks like Bloom’s Taxonomy to design outcomes-based learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical &amp;amp; Consultative Mindset: Ability to translate complex data into actionable enablement initiatives and influence executive stakeholders without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adaptable &amp;amp; Collaborative: A self-starter with a strong sense of urgency, excellent facilitation skills, and a proven ability to build trust across global matrixed teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;This role will be remote and based in Ontario, British Columbia or Alberta, Canada&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We prioritize connection and opportunities to build relationships with our customers and each other. For this role, approximately 15-25% travel is anticipated to help you connect in-person in a meaningful way.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
