&lt;li&gt;Act as the bridge between data engineers, data scientists, analysts, and business stakeholders to translate business needs into data solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop product requirements and user stories focused on data access, usability, performance, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritize data initiatives based on business impact, technical feasibility, and data availability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure proper data governance, privacy, and compliance practices are followed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure teams have self-service access to GTM data via platforms, tools, and interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and improve data quality, reliability, and user adoption of data tools and features, providing regular reporting on effectiveness and areas for improvement..&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and track success metrics for data products, ensuring they meet business and technical goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of data-driven decision making by making data products intuitive and accessible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with finance, product, and sales teams to ensure that data products serve the needs of our internal customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay informed about industry trends, tools, and best practices in data product management and data enablement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop training materials to empower teams across the organization to use data effectively for decision-making, campaign execution, and customer engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead initiatives to improve data literacy across teams, ensuring that data is accessible, understandable, and actionable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities for innovation in how we leverage data, driving new methodologies and technologies to enhance data utilization and customer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
